# Protect the authoritative backend from the friend's branch.
#
# Since the 2026-07-31 folder rename, his UI (`front_end/`) and ours share a path, so
# `git merge origin/UI-experiment2` is finally possible. But merging a branch takes the WHOLE
# branch — and he makes real backend changes too (tax, quotation, handoff logic). Without this,
# a merge silently replays 124 backend files over ours, and `back_end/` is the source of truth
# on both branches.
#
# `merge=ours` tells git to keep OUR version of these paths on every merge, always.
#
# ⚠ THIS ONLY WORKS IF THE MACHINE HAS THE DRIVER REGISTERED. Run once, per clone:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# Without it git silently falls back to a normal merge and his backend WILL land on ours.
# Verify with `git config --get merge.ours.driver` before merging his branch.
back_end/**            merge=ours

# Reference-only snapshot of his backend — we never wire against it, so never let a merge
# rewrite our copy either.
friend_back_end/**     merge=ours

# Ours by definition; his branch has no such folder, but be explicit.
my_front_end/**        merge=ours

# Repo-level docs and operating notes are ours.
CLAUDE.md              merge=ours
docs/**                merge=ours
.claude/**             merge=ours
